Principles of Insurance
Principle of Utmost Good Faith: According to
this principle, insurance is a contract based on
faith. The insured and insurer must disclose all
the material facts to each other and both the
parties should not hide any fact related to
insurance policy from each other. If the insured
hides any material fact from the insurance
company and later on the insurer comes to
know about it, then he can refuse to pay
compensation.
